Clear each KV stream in seq_keep and copy the rollback index with a sequence
Fold-into: upstream/memory

The defects. tests/fuzz/core/run.sh test replays the reproducer of each one.

- seq_keep with one KV stream for each sequence keeps the cells of the other sequences.

  With kv_unified = false, each sequence has its own stream. llama_kv_cache::seq_keep clears only
  the stream of the kept sequence, and the other sequences are in the other streams. Thus their
  cells stay, and the next decode of such a sequence also attends to its old cells.

  The change: seq_keep removes each other sequence from each stream.

  The reproducer: tests/fuzz/core/regress/fuzz_recurrent--kv-keep-streams.

- The copy of a sequence with a pending rollback reads the state before the rollback.

  A pending rollback of the source puts its state in the snapshot group rs_idx[src]. seq_cp gives
  the destination the same cell, but the destination keeps rs_idx 0. The destination then reads
  the state before the rollback, and state_write stops the process on the shared cell ("cannot
  write shared recurrent state with different rollback indices").

  The change: seq_cp copies rs_idx of the source to the destination, as it copies rs_depth.

  The reproducer: tests/fuzz/core/regress/fuzz_recurrent--recurrent-shared-rollback.

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 with the patches of patches/series above this one.

Files:
    src/llama-kv-cache.cpp
    src/llama-memory-recurrent.cpp
--- a/src/llama-kv-cache.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-kv-cache.cpp
@@ -548,22 +548,26 @@ void llama_kv_cache::seq_keep(llama_seq_id seq_id) {
 
     GGML_ASSERT(seq_id >= 0 && (size_t) seq_id < seq_to_stream.size());
 
-    auto & cells = v_cells[seq_to_stream[seq_id]];
-    auto & head  = v_heads[seq_to_stream[seq_id]];
+    // With one stream for each sequence (kv_unified = false), the other sequences are in the
+    // other streams, thus each stream drops every sequence except seq_id.
+    for (uint32_t s = 0; s < n_stream; ++s) {
+        auto & cells = v_cells[s];
+        auto & head  = v_heads[s];
 
-    uint32_t new_head = cells.size();
+        uint32_t new_head = cells.size();
 
-    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < cells.size(); ++i) {
-        if (cells.seq_keep(i, seq_id)) {
-            if (new_head == cells.size()) {
-                new_head = i;
+        for (uint32_t i = 0; i < cells.size(); ++i) {
+            if (cells.seq_keep(i, seq_id)) {
+                if (new_head == cells.size()) {
+                    new_head = i;
+                }
             }
         }
-    }
 
-    // If we freed up a slot, set head to it so searching can start there.
-    if (new_head != cells.size() && new_head < head) {
-        head = new_head;
+        // If we freed up a slot, set head to it so searching can start there.
+        if (new_head != cells.size() && new_head < head) {
+            head = new_head;
+        }
     }
 }
 
--- a/src/llama-memory-recurrent.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-memory-recurrent.cpp
@@ -307,6 +307,14 @@ void llama_memory_recurrent::seq_cp(llama_seq_id seq_id_src, llama_seq_id seq_id
         if ((size_t) seq_id_src < rs_depth.size() && (size_t) seq_id_dst < rs_depth.size()) {
             rs_depth[seq_id_dst] = tail_src.tail >= 0 ? rs_depth[seq_id_src] : 0;
         }
+
+        // A pending rollback of the source puts its state in snapshot group rs_idx[src]. The
+        // destination shares the cell, thus it reads the same group. With rs_idx[dst] = 0 it
+        // reads the state before the rollback, and state_write aborts on the shared cell
+        // ("cannot write shared recurrent state with different rollback indices").
+        if ((size_t) seq_id_src < rs_idx.size() && (size_t) seq_id_dst < rs_idx.size()) {
+            rs_idx[seq_id_dst] = tail_src.tail >= 0 ? rs_idx[seq_id_src] : 0;
+        }
     }
 }
 
